rocket-chip TLB superpage refill: write the entry selected by waddr. With the hypervisor extension
waddr selects the superpage entry that already hit, which the re-walk for a guest-page fault's
guest physical address must refill, but the loop wrote r_superpage_repl_addr instead. A VS/VU
access whose VS-stage leaf is a superpage and whose G-stage translation faults then alternated
walks with need_gpa = 0 and 1 and neither retired nor trapped. The sectored refill below it uses
its waddr. Local patch; no upstream issue or pull request.

diff --git a/src/main/scala/rocket/TLB.scala b/src/main/scala/rocket/TLB.scala
--- a/src/main/scala/rocket/TLB.scala
+++ b/src/main/scala/rocket/TLB.scala
@@ -475,7 +475,7 @@
       special_entry.foreach(_.insert(r_refill_tag, refill_v, io.ptw.resp.bits.level, newEntry))
     }.elsewhen (io.ptw.resp.bits.level < (pgLevels-1).U) {
       val waddr = Mux(r_superpage_hit.valid && usingHypervisor.B, r_superpage_hit.bits, r_superpage_repl_addr)
-      for ((e, i) <- superpage_entries.zipWithIndex) when (r_superpage_repl_addr === i.U) {
+      for ((e, i) <- superpage_entries.zipWithIndex) when (waddr === i.U) {
         e.insert(r_refill_tag, refill_v, io.ptw.resp.bits.level, newEntry)
         when (invalidate_refill) { e.invalidate() }
       }
